# wip — ask-exchange
# Started: 2026-11-06

#>plan_ask_exchange
#:plan #!projection_feedback
#:layer #!pragmatics

@["card"]{
 phase: #seed
 gist: "A mounted consumer's asks reach one intake with a home and status each, a check reports drift, and replies reach it on its next pin"
 touches: [~".agents/plans/first-plugin/wip.spw", ~".agents/plans/inquiry-loop/wip.spw", ~".agents/plans/vscode-lsp-roadmap/PLAN.md"]
 will_touch: [~".spw/exchange"]
 entry: ~"./PLAN.md"
 next: "?[ask_key]: settle how an intake row names an ask without naming the consumer; then ~[intake_shape]."
}

^["edges"]{
 shares: [~"../first-plugin/wip.spw", ~"../inquiry-loop/wip.spw", ~"../ground-edge-reading/wip.spw", ~"../vscode-lsp-roadmap/wip.spw", ~"../onboarding-quest/wip.spw", ~"../reading-drift/wip.spw"]
}

^["roots"]{
 @plan: ~".agents/plans/ask-exchange/PLAN.md"
 @plugin_intake: ~".agents/plans/first-plugin/wip.spw"
 @capability_intake: ~".agents/plans/inquiry-loop/wip.spw"
 @roadmap_table: ~".agents/plans/vscode-lsp-roadmap/PLAN.md"
 @brainstorm: ~".spw/caches/journal/2026-11-06-reading-brainstorm.spw"
}

^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "Asks stop going unread because the table that should hold them is one of four, or its home moved"
 ~#taste: "The consumer owns its asks; the workbench owns a home and a status per ask id; a verb compares the two"
}

^["open"]{
 # Unresolved questions. When resolved: log in stream, then move to ^["done"] as ~#resolved(label).
 ?[ask_key]: "How does an intake row name an ask without naming the consumer: the ask id alone, the id with its theme file (plugins_and_tooling.one_plugin), or a consumer label the consumer's own workspace declares?"
 ?[verb_home]: "spw asks as its own verb, or a doctor check that runs when a mounted consumer is named by path?"
 ?[replies_channel]: "Does the consumer read replies from the mount (.spw/_workbench/.spw/exchange/replies.spw) on its pin bump, or does the check write them into the consumer's scratch for a person to carry?"
}

^["commits"]{
 # Named, in order. Planned ~[name]; landed .[name](hash). Names are never reused.
 ~[intake_shape]: "#[exchange] — .spw/exchange/intake.spw: one row per ask with its key, home plan, status, and the receipt that moved it; no consumer name, no ask text (after ?[ask_key])"
 ~[asks_check_fixture]: "![cli] — a fixture ask tree with one ask homed on an archived plan, one with no row, and one whose status disagrees with its home; the check is red on all three"
 ~[asks_check]: "&[cli] — read a consumer's ask files by explicit path, in their slot order, and report asks with no row, homes that are archived, dormant or rescoped, and statuses that disagree (takes onboarding-quest collect_asks)"
 ~[intake_moves]: "&[plans] — the intake frames in first-plugin, inquiry-loop and ground-edge-reading and the vscode-lsp-roadmap table become citations into the intake"
 ~[pin_age]: "&[cli] — the check reports how far a consumer's pin sits behind main and whether its commit is only on an archived branch; on 2026-11-08 one consumer read 128 commits behind (2026-08-24), so every fix since was absent from its lint and its vendored bundle"
 ~[replies_file]: "#[exchange] — .spw/exchange/replies.spw: misroutes, stale claims and facts that did not reproduce, starting from inquiry-loop ^replies (after ?[replies_channel])"
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-11-06 17:24] observe — Consumer asks reach this repo through four tables in four shapes: first-plugin ^intake (ranks 1 to 17), inquiry-loop ^intake (capability asks), ground-edge-reading ^intake (motions asks) and the vscode-lsp-roadmap PLAN.md table (the 2026-10-12 review). The motions asks were routed to a plan rescoped before they were filed and stayed unread from 2026-10-27 to 2026-11-06; five roadmap rows stayed stale after their work landed.
 >>[2026-11-06 17:24] decide — A plan of its own, taking onboarding-quest collect_asks, since an asks check serves every consumer ask and not only the quest's. The workbench keeps no consumer text and names no consumer, as mounted-consumer-tooling and ecosystem-surface-governance already require.
 >>[2026-11-08 09:47] observe — Two arrivals on 2026-11-08 came through no ask file. A second mounted consumer's review reached the owner as chat; its homes: unreserved valence words and lint failing on degradation (plan-stream-parse-health), one reader with three profiles (line-kit, parser-releases), roles not namespaces, provenance, clause authority and comparison (interpretation-trials), task verbs (cli-sense-reorientation ?[task_verbs]), fixtures from use (reading-drift, host-receipts), registers (syntax-hardware-alignment). The site's plane reports (2026-11-07) record 16 workbench asks in the site's own plan, not in its upstream file; homes: one operator descriptor (audit-ui-data-models), codec, splitter and body-join reader (line-kit), the pentad's three readings (interpretation-trials wonder_trial_valence_word), runtime and theory asks without a home yet (next entry).
 >>[2026-11-08 09:47] note — ?[ask_key] now has two consumers to key without naming either, and a source that is no file (an owner's chat). pin_age added: a consumer reading a stale pin reports problems main has fixed or never had.
 >>[2026-11-08 09:48] note — Unhomed from the plane reports: the physics report's runtime asks (! of a deferral returns it and writes a * receipt; an unanswered ? stays a value, not null; . with no path lowers an integrated value to its parts; the operator descriptor carries what a mark closes into) and the ground report's theory asks (an order parameter for bonk; whether plane is a valence noun; a law for valence carried on register writes; keeping the physics-flavor sentence without hostnames). The first two runtime asks are kin to wonder_trial_prime_actualize; the descriptor ask joins audit-ui-data-models. A runtime-semantics home is the owner's call.
 >>[2026-11-09 18:12] note — Routing on 2026-11-09. Site consumer: ranks 18 to 21 to inquiry-loop and first-plugin; valence_charge to wonder_trial_valence_word; asks kept only in its caches (pairs and depth as data, one release every consumer takes, a lite profile kit, sockets first, ranges with units, holes, an address codec, juxtaposition and streams) to line-kit, parser-releases, first-plugin and syntax-hardware-alignment. Second consumer: it keeps no reviews folder; its asks live in three surfaces of its own canon (nine asks, ten proposals dated 2026-11-09, fifteen stress findings), and its pin is main at edbc5500. Both keep asks outside any file this repo reads on a schedule, which is the case for ask_key and pin_age.
 >>[2026-11-12 09:19] note — Unhomed on 2026-11-12, from the site consumer's capability asks as read in journal 2026-11-11-entrypoints-and-dreaming: turns_that_land (its rank 9) appears here only inside a trial card's readers_today, and seeded_mosey (its rank 10) appears in no plan. Proposed homes, not yet routed: turns_that_land to line-kit slot_edits with parse-columns' rhymes as the index of where a turn lands (line-kit stream 2026-11-12); seeded_mosey beside caches-living-tree ~[wander_journal] and the plan index's wander door, since each is a walk a seed makes repeatable. inquiry_loop (its rank 1) is already owned by inquiry-loop.
 >>[2026-11-12 09:25] note — Sharpening the 09:19 entry: turns_that_land (rank 9) and seeded_mosey (rank 10) are ranked in the site consumer's corpus-and-cli recommendations list, and inquiry_loop (rank 1) in its capabilities list; the ranks are per list, as editor-reading-hierarchy's 2026-10-25 entry uses 9 and 10 from another.
}

